WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.253
- I give, always, an honor to
being here for the Braves.

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:05.255
My dream was to be a big
leaguer with the Braves,

00:00:05.255 --> 00:00:06.297
and I accomplished that.

00:00:06.297 --> 00:00:09.259
So, to me, it's like I'm
living the dream right now.

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:11.886
And that's when I got my
tattoo literally saying that.

00:00:11.886 --> 00:00:13.138
- OK.
- I had to.

00:00:13.138 --> 00:00:17.308
I had to, because everything
was like it was meant to be

00:00:17.308 --> 00:00:18.643
at that point.

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:21.813
[Funky upbeat music]

00:00:26.818 --> 00:00:30.238
[Funky upbeat music]

00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:34.868
- Ozzie, what's goin’ on?

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:38.747
We are here at Good Kitchen +
Market in Marietta, Georgia.

00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:40.540
Why this place of all places?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.125
- Well, I have to take you guys here

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:45.045
because this is one of the
best breakfast/lunch spots

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:45.879
I come to.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.589
- What are the top things on
the menu that we should get?

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:48.423
You mentioned breakfast.

00:00:48.423 --> 00:00:51.426
- So, breakfast, I go
always with plain pancakes.

00:00:51.426 --> 00:00:52.260
I like plain pancakes.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.471
Some three Italian meatballs.

00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:55.305
- [Granderson:] OK.

00:00:55.305 --> 00:00:56.139
- That's what I like in the morning.

00:00:56.139 --> 00:00:56.973
- [Granderson:] So pancake and meatball?

00:00:56.973 --> 00:00:58.224
- Meatballs. I really like the pancakes here.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.059
- OK.

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.226
- My favorite spot for pancakes.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.937
- Now is this the go-to
place all the time?

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:04.564
- We come back home from a road trip,

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.774
and we have seven games here,

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:07.400
I come here at least three, four times

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.234
in that week.
- OK.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:12.280
Now, obviously Atlanta is
your home away from home.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.532
This is where you play,
this is where you’ve won,

00:01:14.532 --> 00:01:16.242
but this isn't where you're from.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:19.120
- So, I'm originally from Curaçao.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.497
- [Granderson:] All right.
And where is Curaçao located?

00:01:20.497 --> 00:01:22.749
- Curaçao is in South America.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:25.877
It's close located to Venezuela.
- [Granderson:] All right.
- Aruba.

00:01:25.877 --> 00:01:29.798
And I mean, just being born
from there and growing up there,

00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:31.466
it's one of the best things.

00:01:31.466 --> 00:01:32.550
You know, you're on the island,

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.719
but there's so much fun stuff to do.

00:01:34.719 --> 00:01:37.388
You go off-roading, you
go fishing, swimming,

00:01:37.388 --> 00:01:38.348
all those great stuff.

00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:40.183
- So, being in Curaçao,

00:01:40.183 --> 00:01:42.477
a little bit of the
knowledge I know about it,

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:44.187
and we're sitting here speaking in English,

00:01:44.187 --> 00:01:45.605
but this isn't your native language.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:46.439
- [Chuckling] I know.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.273
- You know, what's your native language?

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.484
What's the native language
spoken in Curaçao?

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:51.402
- My native language is Papiamentu.

00:01:51.402 --> 00:01:53.363
It's spoken there, Aruba and Bonaire.

00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:54.197
- OK.

00:01:54.197 --> 00:01:55.115
- So those ABC islands.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:55.949
- All right.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:57.242
- That's where it's mainly spoken.

00:01:57.242 --> 00:01:58.660
- English has to come into the mix.
- Yes.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.286
- When does English get introduced?

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.121
- So, when you go to school,

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:03.957
it's mandatory to learn these languages

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:04.791
- OK.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.292
- So you go to school, you still learn Papiamentu.
- Uh-huh.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.920
- Cuz, you know you're a little kid. You’re starting to talk.
- Right.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.756
- And then you have English, Spanish, Dutch.

00:02:11.756 --> 00:02:13.091
- If we're going to eat here,

00:02:13.091 --> 00:02:14.926
and I want you to order in Papiamentu,

00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:17.387
how do you order what
you're gonna order today?

00:02:17.387 --> 00:02:18.221
- So if—

00:02:18.221 --> 00:02:19.347
- The pancakes, the meatballs.

00:02:19.347 --> 00:02:22.809
- OK, let's do the pancake,
meatballs with bacon and eggs.
- OK.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:23.977
- So I will say,

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.103
“Bon dia.”

00:02:25.103 --> 00:02:26.855
That means “good morning.”
- All right.

00:02:26.855 --> 00:02:29.232
- Mi ke webu, speki

00:02:29.232 --> 00:02:31.901
meatball ku pancake

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:32.819
- All right.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:33.653
- Just like that.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:34.571
- Translate it straight through.

00:02:34.571 --> 00:02:35.989
So it’d be the pancakes with the eggs.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:40.034
- Yeah, pancake with the
eggs, with bacon and meatball.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:42.662
- [Announcer:] Swing and a drive!

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.454
[Crowd cheering]

00:02:43.454 --> 00:02:48.084
Deep right field! Ozzie Albies
hit it in the Chop House!

00:02:48.084 --> 00:02:50.086
- [Granderson:] Now,
did you watch baseball

00:02:50.086 --> 00:02:51.337
growing up?
- Yes, always.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.172
- OK. You were a big fan at that time?

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.006
- Big fan, yes.

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:54.215
- Favorite team growing up?

00:02:54.215 --> 00:02:55.091
- Favorite team,

00:02:55.091 --> 00:02:56.885
so me and my grandfather used to watch,

00:02:56.885 --> 00:02:58.011
every night, baseball games,

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.470
and we watched the Braves and the Dodgers.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:00.346
- OK.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.139
- Every night.

00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:01.973
- Nice.

00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:02.849
- That's what his favorite teams were.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:06.561
So, Braves became my favorite
team because of my grandfather.

00:03:06.561 --> 00:03:08.021
- Mmhmm. One of my favorite
teams as well.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.773
One of my favorite players,
also a Curaçao native,

00:03:10.773 --> 00:03:11.774
Andruw Jones.
- Andruw Jones.

00:03:11.774 --> 00:03:12.734
You guys played together.

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.235
- Was he a reason, you know,

00:03:14.235 --> 00:03:15.570
that you liked watching the Braves—
- Yes!

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:16.905
- Your grandfather liked
watching the Braves?

00:03:16.905 --> 00:03:21.159
- Big reason. A big reason why we
always watched the Braves,

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:22.952
because of Andruw Jones.

00:03:22.952 --> 00:03:24.454
You know, we had Hensley Meulens
too, Bam Bam Meulens.

00:03:25.455 --> 00:03:28.041
But Andruw Jones, everybody
was—when I grew up,

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:30.168
everybody Andruw Jones,
Andruw Jones, Andruw Jones.
- [Granderson:] Yeah.

00:03:30.168 --> 00:03:32.003
- So, I even have a picture with him.

00:03:32.003 --> 00:03:33.296
- [Granderson:] Ah. How old were
you when you got that picture?

00:03:33.296 --> 00:03:34.130
- Five years old.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:36.007
I just turned five on that same day.

00:03:36.007 --> 00:03:37.759
And my dad surprised me,
the picture with him.

00:03:37.759 --> 00:03:40.094
- So, at that time, you're five years old,

00:03:40.094 --> 00:03:43.431
and Curaçao is growing
and getting on the map,

00:03:43.431 --> 00:03:46.184
the baseball map.
- Mmhmm.
- You got Andruw Jones doing his thing

00:03:46.184 --> 00:03:47.018
in the major leagues.

00:03:47.018 --> 00:03:47.852
- Yes.

00:03:47.852 --> 00:03:49.938
- But you also have the
Little League World Series

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:52.357
being represented by your country,

00:03:52.357 --> 00:03:53.650
the Senior League World Series.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.360
Like, teams from your country,

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.820
players that you might know or know of,

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.657
are playing at the highest
level for the world to see.

00:04:00.657 --> 00:04:02.158
Was that influential for you?

00:04:02.158 --> 00:04:03.701
- Yes, it was. Yes, it was.

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:05.536
So, like I said, started with Andruw Jones,

00:04:05.536 --> 00:04:08.665
but then you heard of
Andrelton Simmons coming up,

00:04:08.665 --> 00:04:11.376
Roger Bernadina, all these guys coming,

00:04:11.376 --> 00:04:13.628
and Profar, Schoop.

00:04:13.628 --> 00:04:18.216
And out of nowhere, something
was, like, in my mind. Like, hey,

00:04:18.216 --> 00:04:21.344
I wanna be a major league
baseball player one day, too.

00:04:21.344 --> 00:04:22.178
- [Announcer:] Ozzie Albies,

00:04:22.178 --> 00:04:24.931
one of the most aggressive
hitters in all of baseball.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.266
The slide, he's safe!

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:27.350
[Crowd cheering]

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:28.977
Oh, my goodness!

00:04:28.977 --> 00:04:30.603
- [Announcer:] Think they're
fired up at Truist Park?

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:31.437
You betcha.

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:36.359
- So take me through last year:
The Braves are gettin' hot.

00:04:37.193 --> 00:04:39.279
We enter the playoffs.

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:42.282
How was that just from
a mental standpoint?

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:44.701
For you personally, for the team?

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:46.494
You know, how did that all unfold?

00:04:46.494 --> 00:04:49.998
- The year before, we lost in the NLCS.
- Yeah.

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:53.835
And we were like, "OK,
this year is our year.

00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:56.170
We have to go for it, and
we have to win whole thing.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:58.172
We're not gonna just be
in it. We have to win.”

00:04:58.172 --> 00:04:59.716
So going into it mentally,

00:04:59.716 --> 00:05:03.344
you know, you work the whole
season for these moments.

00:05:03.344 --> 00:05:04.178
- Yeah.
- So when we got there,

00:05:04.178 --> 00:05:05.972
it's all about “Let's go take care of

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:07.348
what we need to take care of.”
- Right.

00:05:07.348 --> 00:05:09.350
“Don't think about the
roads we're gonna face,

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:14.105
all the people, the teams.
Let's go just focus on us.”

00:05:14.105 --> 00:05:17.608
We did that. And like everybody saw,

00:05:17.608 --> 00:05:19.444
that's what got us to the World Series.

00:05:19.444 --> 00:05:20.945
Now we're here together as one team.

00:05:20.945 --> 00:05:21.904
And that's what we did.

00:05:21.904 --> 00:05:24.157
- [Granderson:] So you won together.

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:27.076
- Oh, yes. Won together. We couldn't
do it by ourselves, the only chance.

00:05:27.076 --> 00:05:29.037
- How was the celebration?

00:05:29.037 --> 00:05:29.871
- Ooh. [Chuckling]

00:05:29.871 --> 00:05:31.789
- In Atlanta, you win the World Series.

00:05:31.789 --> 00:05:33.791
This is the hope and dream of kids

00:05:33.791 --> 00:05:34.876
that wanna play baseball.
- Yes, yes.

00:05:34.876 --> 00:05:36.586
- And now you've just accomplished it.

00:05:36.586 --> 00:05:38.546
- Just get to the World
Series, getting there,

00:05:38.546 --> 00:05:39.714
was the biggest thing for me.
- Yeah.

00:05:39.714 --> 00:05:41.924
- Cuz you always see this on TV.

00:05:41.924 --> 00:05:43.760
You've never been there physically.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:45.636
Like, oh yeah, the World Series.

00:05:45.636 --> 00:05:47.805
But being there, as soon
as I step in Houston,

00:05:47.805 --> 00:05:49.140
I remember, first game, I look around.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:50.600
I was like, “This is it.”

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.434
- Were you nervous?

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:52.268
- No.
- No? OK.

00:05:52.268 --> 00:05:53.436
- I was excited.

00:05:53.436 --> 00:05:54.395
Excitement like,

00:05:54.395 --> 00:05:57.940
“OK, here is what I worked
my whole life for, the ring.”

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:58.775
- Yeah.

00:05:58.775 --> 00:06:00.985
- And went in,

00:06:00.985 --> 00:06:04.447
I remember getting into the
first when I got the stolen base.

00:06:04.447 --> 00:06:06.908
I’m like, “This is really happening.”
- Mmhmm.

00:06:06.908 --> 00:06:09.243
- I couldn't believe it.

00:06:09.243 --> 00:06:12.497
So, I would say one of the most
amazing moments in my life, the World Series.

00:06:12.497 --> 00:06:13.539
- [Granderson:] That's awesome.

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:15.249
How was it when you went back home?

00:06:15.249 --> 00:06:16.626
- When I went back home,

00:06:16.626 --> 00:06:18.252
they did a whole parade just for me.

00:06:18.252 --> 00:06:19.087
- Soon as you land?

00:06:19.087 --> 00:06:23.049
- As soon as I land, they put
me on one of those big cars—
- Yeah.

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:25.885
- And just drive me through
the whole Curaçao.

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:27.387
- Wow. Everybody came out to see you?

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:29.847
- Every—oh, my God, it was an amazing moment.
- That’s awesome.

00:06:29.847 --> 00:06:31.849
It was a whole parade, just me on there.

00:06:33.101 --> 00:06:35.520
[Rhythmic music]

00:06:38.606 --> 00:06:42.193
- There were also four
other Curaçao players

00:06:42.193 --> 00:06:43.903
that played for the Braves before you.

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:44.737
- Yes.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:47.824
- Randall Simon, Andrelton
Simmons, Andruw Jones,

00:06:47.824 --> 00:06:49.867
Jair Jurrjens. You're the fifth.

00:06:49.867 --> 00:06:51.702
You get a sixth Curaçao player,

00:06:51.702 --> 00:06:52.537
- Exactly. [Laughing]

00:06:52.537 --> 00:06:53.371
- Kenley Jansen.

00:06:53.371 --> 00:06:54.205
- Yes.

00:06:54.205 --> 00:06:55.706
- [Granderson:] Joins you and the Braves.

00:06:55.706 --> 00:06:57.208
- I remember him calling me and saying,

00:06:57.208 --> 00:06:58.334
"Hey, I signed with the Braves.”

00:06:58.334 --> 00:06:59.210
I said, “Perfect.”
- Nice.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:00.044
- “Let's go,

00:07:00.044 --> 00:07:02.046
and let's go to win the World
Series this year together.”

00:07:02.046 --> 00:07:04.090
That's what, that's our goal right now.

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:06.342
And he got to Atlanta.

00:07:06.342 --> 00:07:08.302
I show him some cool restaurants.

00:07:08.302 --> 00:07:11.264
We go together, we eat, we enjoy.

00:07:11.264 --> 00:07:13.850
Travel with the team,
we sit together, talk.

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:16.185
You know, always have
fun with a group of guys

00:07:16.185 --> 00:07:18.563
playing Uno and all
this stuff on the plane.

00:07:18.563 --> 00:07:22.024
But I really liked the way—

00:07:22.024 --> 00:07:23.443
first time it ever happened to me too,

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:26.279
having a Curaçao guy on the same team.

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:28.823
So, it was actually a great moment

00:07:28.823 --> 00:07:30.116
for him to be on the team.

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:32.160
He came, he actually came to the
restaurant here with me, too.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:32.994
- OK. You brought him here?

00:07:32.994 --> 00:07:34.537
- We ate here together, too.

00:07:34.537 --> 00:07:36.205
- Do you remember what
you had to eat that day?

00:07:36.205 --> 00:07:38.124
- Pancakes and everything.

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:39.876
He loves pancakes also.
- Good, good.

00:07:39.876 --> 00:07:43.212
- And, you know, he's a big boy.
he likes to eat this whole thing.

00:07:43.212 --> 00:07:44.839
- [Granderson:] Winning one is great.
- Mmhmm.

00:07:44.839 --> 00:07:46.466
- But winning two would be even better.

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:48.426
Kenley has a ring with the Dodgers.

00:07:48.426 --> 00:07:50.511
You have a ring with the Braves.

00:07:50.511 --> 00:07:52.096
You two getting two rings together?

00:07:52.096 --> 00:07:53.055
- That would be amazing.

00:07:53.055 --> 00:07:56.017
It's gonna be the
biggest parade in Curaçao

00:07:56.017 --> 00:07:57.560
if that happened.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:58.978
It would be amazing.

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:00.521
We gotta go get it together now.
- Right.

00:08:00.521 --> 00:08:01.606
- We're on the same team.

00:08:01.606 --> 00:08:02.857
Let's make history. Let's go!

00:08:02.857 --> 00:08:06.068
- Continue to do
it and live that dream, that tattoo.

00:08:06.068 --> 00:08:06.903
- Always.

00:08:06.903 --> 00:08:07.778
- Let me see that tattoo one more time.

00:08:07.778 --> 00:08:08.863
- Always, always.

00:08:08.863 --> 00:08:09.697
- Live the dream.

00:08:09.697 --> 00:08:10.531
- Always.

00:08:10.531 --> 00:08:11.491
I will always do that.

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:12.450
- Keep living the dream.
- I will.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:13.993
- It's been an absolute pleasure.

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:14.827
- Thank you so much.

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:15.745
- And thanks for the recommendation.
- Mmhmm.

00:08:15.745 --> 00:08:19.373
- When I'm in Marietta, I'm
coming to Good Kitchen + Market,

00:08:19.373 --> 00:08:20.833
and I'm gonna get the pancakes next time.

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:21.959
- Yes, please.
- All right.

00:08:21.959 --> 00:08:22.752
- You'll enjoy it.

